// Sleep n steps of ~20ms by draining the serial port n times: each drain
// call blocks in a 20ms-timeout read (go/b/ser/drain/pull.id) rather than
// sleeping first and draining after, so a burst that arrives partway through
// the "sleep" is caught as soon as it arrives rather than up to one whole
// step late -- the closest this can come, with no threads, to qmon.py's
// background reader, which never stopped reading at all.
wait_loop(int n) {
  int i = 0;
  while(i < n) {
    i = wait_step(i);
  }
} return void;

wait_step(int i) {
  drain_serial();
  int j = i + 1;
} return int j;
